      "id": "update-ready",
      "status": "pending",
      "surface": "Installed update-ready banner",
      "proof": "Unsigned Squirrel update, version, release link, Later and Restart actions. Reached only through the process-local verification seam (MATERIAL_COOKIE_CLICKER_VERIFY_UPDATE_FEED), which requires a deterministic prior<candidate<target Squirrel feed served over bounded credential-free HTTPS that Windows' real certificate validation will trust. No such feed exists on this machine or task boundary, and standing one up needs either a certificate authority-issued TLS certificate (this repository permanently prohibits obtaining or holding signing material of any kind, and a locally-issued self-signed cert is not something Squirrel's HTTPS client will accept) or a public host, neither of which is available in this session. Left pending rather than forcing an insecure or fabricated feed."
    },
    {
      "id": "installed-launch",
      "status": "pending",
      "surface": "Installed executable launch",
      "proof": "Installed executable launched on a named hidden desktop with packaged icon visible. scripts/prepare-squirrel-runtime-verification.mjs states the install boundary plainly: 'disposable operating-system user or disposable VM; LOCALAPPDATA redirection is forbidden'. This machine's %LOCALAPPDATA%\\MaterialCookieClicker already holds a real prior installation (app-0.2.50/0.2.52/0.2.55) from earlier sessions; installing this task's older 0.2.0 Setup.exe over or beside it on the single shared user account risks corrupting or shadowing that install, and no disposable Windows user or VM is available to this task to isolate the install as the project's own contract requires. Creating a new local OS user account to obtain that isolation is a system-account change outside this task's authority. Left pending rather than installing into a shared, non-disposable location."
    },
    {
      "id": "event-pool-remaining",
      "status": "pending",
      "surface": "Remaining event pool",
      "proof": "Confirmed unreachable in the current build, not merely unphotographed: src/shared/game/reducer.ts#handleTick computes `blocked: goldenCookie.isSpawned || nextState.minigames.active !== null`, but `minigames.active` is `undefined` on a fresh save (and never becomes exactly `null` afterward), and `undefined !== null` is `true` in JavaScript. tickRandomEvents is therefore called with blocked:true on every tick, forever, so the pool can never spawn a single event. Verified live: a save satisfying every unlock threshold, with the developer flag `material-cookie-clicker:events:fast=event:sprinkle_storm` set, never spawned over 60+s of real ticking while the persisted save's randomEvents.rngStreamIndex and nextEligibleAtEpochMs stayed frozen at 0 and the cookie balance and goldenCookie.rngStreamIndex both visibly advanced in the same window. Flagged out-of-scope (this lane may not touch src/) as a spawned task suggesting the one-line fix (`!== undefined`)."
    },
